== Criterion 3b — a bare `go test` build has Commit == "unknown", NO fallback to vcs.revision ==
The branch's own test files do NOT pin this (see FINDING F1). Proven with two throwaway probes
placed in bf1-check/internal/version/zz_probe_test.go (scratch copy only; discarded):
cmd: cd bf1-check && go test -count=1 -v -run 'TestProbe_' ./internal/version/
out: TestProbe_BareBuildCommitUnknown:
       bare build: Commit="unknown" VCSRevision="" VCSModified=false   --- PASS
     TestProbe_NoFallbackToVCSRevision (injects readBuildInfo with vcs.revision=deadbeefcafe1234
       and vcs.modified=true, then calls Get()):
       no fallback: Commit="unknown" while VCSRevision="deadbeefcafe1234"   --- PASS
     PROBE_EXIT=0
Source confirms the contract: internal/version/version.go Get() sets `Commit: Commit` only; the
vcs.* switch (lines 49-58) writes VCSRevision/VCSTime/VCSModified and never touches info.Commit.

